1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,340
Every day, small businesses across India miss customer calls.

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:08,250
The owner is busy at the counter, the shop has closed for the night,

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,680
or two phones ring at once.

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,500
Each missed call can be a booking that goes to the shop next door.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,580
Alaap is an AI front desk for these shops.

6
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:21,790
It answers phone calls, WhatsApp and web chat in Hindi, Punjabi and English,

7
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,920
the way customers actually speak.

8
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:26,170
It books appointments, takes orders,

9
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,780
and passes anything it can't solve to the owner.

10
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:33,500
Here's a live call to a demo salon. The caller's voice is synthesized;

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,380
everything else is the live app.

12
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:42,540
Riya: Sat Sri Akal! This is Riya from Glow Unisex Salon. This call is recorded. How can I help?

13
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:50,900
Caller: Sat Sri Akal. Can I get a gents haircut tomorrow at 6:30 pm? My name is Rohit.

14
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:52,580
Riya: Hello, Rohit ji!

15
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:54,400
Riya: There's a free slot for a haircut tomorrow at 6:30 pm.

16
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,380
Riya: Could you tell me your 10-digit mobile number?

17
00:00:56,420 --> 00:01:01,320
Riya: Then I'll confirm the booking.

18
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:08,020
Caller: My number is 98123 45670.

19
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:15,020
Riya: Okay Rohit ji: tomorrow 6:30 pm, haircut with Gurpreet, ₹200. Shall I confirm it?

20
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,980
Caller: Yes, please confirm it.

21
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:21,790
Riya: Done!

22
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:23,810
Riya: Your booking number is 5161. A WhatsApp confirmation is on its way.

23
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:29,010
Riya: Anything else I can help with, Rohit ji?

24
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:33,270
The booking lands in the owner's dashboard right away, with the customer's name,

25
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:34,350
number and reference.

26
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:38,470
A WhatsApp confirmation and a reminder are queued automatically.

27
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:42,410
WhatsApp isn't connected in this demo, so they wait in the outbox.

28
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,570
The voice runs on Gnani AI.

29
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:50,290
Gnani's Prisma speech recognition streams the caller's audio in real time,

30
00:01:50,290 --> 00:01:53,760
understands Hindi, Punjabi, English and code-mixed speech,

31
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:56,750
and detects when the caller has finished speaking.

32
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:00,460
Gnani's Timbre text-to-speech gives the assistant its voice,

33
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,170
streamed sentence by sentence,

34
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:06,330
so it starts talking while the rest of the reply is still being prepared.

35
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:08,680
Owners run it in plain language.

36
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:12,610
Asking it to make the facial nine hundred rupees updates the price list.

37
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:17,340
New shops are set up in minutes: paste a rate card or a photo,

38
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:21,650
and the language model reads the services, prices and hours for review.

39
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:25,230
Under the hood: FastAPI and Next.js,

40
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:29,030
with Gnani for speech and Google Gemini for reasoning.

41
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:33,380
Nothing is booked until the customer hears a read-back and says yes.

42
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,410
Row locks prevent double bookings,

43
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:38,450
and forty-four automated tests guard the behaviour.

44
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:43,290
Alaap gives every small shop a front desk that never misses a call,

45
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:46,970
speaks its customers' language, and never invents a price.

46
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:49,350
Alaap. Har call ka jawab.
